<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n323" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγαμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unmarried, single,</i> prop.
			of the man, whether bachelor or widower (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνανδρος</span> being used of the woman), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				9.7
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶ δὲ Τίμωνος βίον, ἄγαμον, ἄδουλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.Com.
					18
				</span></i>
			:—of the woman, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				143
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1502
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				205
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως</span> Sch. ad loc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμος ἄ.</span>”
				<i>marriage that is no marriage, fatal marriage,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1214
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				690
			</span></i>.</div>
